# Testing Rules

Use:

- Vitest for unit tests
- NestJS testing tools for API tests
- Playwright for web end to end tests
- Testcontainers or isolated Docker services for database integration tests where practical

Every business rule must have tests.

High priority test areas:

- Authentication
- Ward code validation
- Authorization
- Household relationships
- Audience membership
- Audience overlap
- Recipient deduplication
- Consent enforcement
- Campaign status transitions
- Idempotent sending
- Provider failure isolation
- Audit creation
- Minor data access restrictions

Use generated fictional data only.

Tests must not depend on execution order.

Do not mock the domain layer when testing application services unless isolation is specifically required.
